{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779656478,"nonce":"B9lyQCV39kdWVFzOCnISriExEYk=","message":"Review found that the shell CLI is mostly layout-aware: it finds the worktree for the target branch and stores that path as auth request cwd. The concrete weak spot is server-side fallback metadata: src/routes/auth.ts derives repo with path.basename(cwd), so a request submitted from a protected branch worktree like .../feedbax/worktrees/develop can be recorded as repo 'develop' unless the CLI supplied repo. I am going to patch the route fallback to derive repo/target_repo_root from git common-dir when cwd is available, with a regression test.","files":null}]}